 result←object New arg;parent;name;props;newobj;∆separator;from;vars;p;pname;∆style
⍝ The APL+Win Menu class may generate one or more of four different Dyalog classes (MenuBar, Menu, MenuItem, Separator), depending on usage

 (parent name)←object ⍝ Separate non-standard two-part argument
 (∆separator ∆style)←arg ##._supp.GetInitialProps'separator' 'style'
 arg,⍨←(~arg ##._supp.HasInitialProps'caption')/⊂'caption'name ⍝ If they're not setting a caption immediately at all, we'll put in a default ⍝? Can they use "&"?

 from←parent ⋄ :While 0≠from.⎕NC'_Owner' ⋄ from←from._Owner ⋄ :EndWhile ⍝ Find logical parent
 props←'MenuItem' ⍝ Default to a MenuItem, but it might need to be converted to a Menu later if it gets its own children
 :Select from._class
 :CaseList 'Form' 'MDIForm'
     :If ~'_mb'⊂⍛∊##.##.LeafName¨##.##.∆WN⍕parent ⍝ If we're not already attaching to a MenuBar object...
         parent←⎕VGET(from⍕⍛,'._mb')##.##.∆WC'MenuBar' ⍝ ...then we need to create one to hold all our menus
         parent._Owner←from ⋄ parent.⎕WX←0 ⍝? Any other invisible initializations?
     :Else
         parent←⎕VGET from⍕⍛,'._mb' ⍝ Point to the existing MenuBar for my internal parent
     :EndIf
 :Case 'Menu'
⍝? May change the internal Dyalog class of the parent; watch out if being deleted later?
     :Select parent ##.##.∆WG'Type' ⍝ We may need to adjust our parent Dyalog type before continuing
     :Case 'MenuBar' ⍝ This cannot accept a Separator child, but otherwise it's fine
         '∆WI DOMAIN ERROR: separator'##.##.Error ∆separator
     :Case 'MenuItem' ⍝ This needs to be converted to a Menu object
         ⍝ Fortunately, I don't think this can have any children yet (except a Timer or BitMap) ⍝? Be careful, just in case
         ⍝? But watch out later if the only child is deleted - should we consider changing it back? It probably will never be used afterwards anyway.
         ⍝? What happens if we already have an onClick handler assigned here?
         ⍝ In order to recreate, we need to first capture all the important information so we can reproduce it
         pname←⍕parent ⍝ We'll keep the name around for reuse after erasing the object
         vars←parent ⎕VGET 2 9 ⍝ Capture all our local variables (and namespaces?) for reproduction ⍝? If it has GUI child objects, do something extra with EWC!
         p←'Caption' 'Posn' 'Active' 'Accelerator' 'Event' ⋄ p←↓p,⍤0⊢parent ##.##.∆WG p ⍝ Capture all the important properties
         ##.##.∆EX⍕parent ⋄ parent←⎕VGET pname ##.##.∆WC'Menu'⊂⍛,p ⍝ Kill the old one and recreate it so it will accept children
         parent ⎕VSET vars ⍝ Make sure the new one knows all the things that the original one did
⍝? What happens in APL+Win if a leaf Menu has onClick or separator or style bits/value and it gets a child afterwards?
⍝? Caption, separator remains but gets ignored. onClick, style, value continues operating normally
     :Case 'Separator' ⍝ We must first convert this into a Menu (non-Separator) object
         pname←⍕parent ⍝ We'll keep the name around for reuse after erasing the object
         vars←parent ⎕VGET 2 9 ⍝ Capture all our local variables (and namespaces?) for reproduction
         p←'Posn' 'Event' ⋄ p←↓p,⍤0⊢parent ##.##.∆WG p ⍝ Capture all the important properties
         ##.##.∆EX⍕parent ⋄ parent←⎕VGET pname ##.##.∆WC'Menu'⊂⍛,p ⍝ Kill the old one and recreate it so it will accept children
         parent ⎕VSET vars ⍝ Make sure the new one knows all the things that the original one did
         {}parent caption,⊂(parent ⎕VGET⊂'_caption'(##.##.LeafName pname)) ⍝ Re-instantiate the original caption
         ⍝? What about a shortcut key (→Accelerator)?
         ⍝ If we delete this child later, this separator flag is retained but it doesn't actually turn back into a Separator.
     :EndSelect
     :If ∆separator ⋄ props←'Separator' ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ They've told us this will be a separator up front, so we'll override it's starting Type
 :Else
     ⍝ Almost any control (or System) can contain a hidden menu activated by a shortcut key or PopUp
     props←'Menu' ⍝ APL+Win pop-up menus must include children to be usable, so we might as well assume that here
 :EndSelect
 props←⊂props
 props,←(~∆separator)/⊂'Style'('Check' 'Radio'⊃⍨1+4∊∆style)           ⍝? Create-only

 newobj←⎕VGET(parent⍕⍛,'.',name)##.##.∆WC props ⍝ Create the actual Dyalog object
 newobj.(_size _extent _where)←⍬ ⍬ ⍬ ⍝ This is an immovable object ⍝? Will these ⍬s hurt any assumptions that are made elsewhere?
 result←parent newobj ##.##.New.Initialize arg ⍝ Complete standard class-initialization procedure
